         'svc.dental-implants.step1': 'Assessment and scan to plan exactly where the implant goes.',
         'svc.dental-implants.step2': 'The implant is placed and the gum is closed over it.',
         'svc.dental-implants.step3': 'Three to six months while the bone fuses to the implant.',
         'svc.dental-implants.step4': 'An impression is taken for your permanent crown.',
         'svc.dental-implants.step5': 'The crown is fitted and your bite is adjusted.',
         'svc.dental-implants.aftercare': 'Expect some swelling and discomfort for two to three days after placement; ice and the painkillers we prescribe are usually enough. Stick to soft food and avoid chewing on that side for the first week. Do not smoke during healing, as it is the single biggest cause of implant failure. Once the crown is fitted, clean it like a natural tooth and keep your six-month checks.',
         'svc.dental-implants.fact1.label': 'Total treatment time',
